  So: old wheel reproduced byte-for-byte, new wheel differs only by the metadata this entry adds, and
  the 29 → 843 METADATA-line jump is README.md being absorbed. Nothing here needed a "roughly".

  One rename hazard that turned out not to exist: if any module called `importlib.metadata.version("myna")`
  at import, the new dist name would have raised `PackageNotFoundError` on every install.
  `grep -rn "importlib|__version__|pkg_resources" src/myna/*.py` prints **nothing** — no code reads its
  own distribution name, which is also why `[project.scripts]` still resolves after the rename.

